      "text": "The midpoint of $s_1$ is $\\left(\\dfrac{4 + (-8)}{2},\\dfrac{1+5}{2}\\right)=(\\boxed{-2,3})$.\n\n## Notes:\n\nTo find the midpoint of a line segment, we use the midpoint formula:\n$$M=\\left(\\frac{x_1+x_2}{2},\\frac{y_1+y_2}{2}\\right)$$\nIn this case, the coefficients of $x_1$ and $x_2$ cancel out, resulting in the simplified formula:\n$$M=\\left(\\frac{x+y}{2},\\frac{x+y}{2}\\right)$$",
